  "caveats": [
   "Cell elites are selected by held-out error among 45k+ unique candidates, so the champion values carry selection (winner's curse) bias; the CMA-ES search itself optimizes only the search-set error.",
   "Tier labels are mechanical insertion-time comparisons against the then-incumbent, not a validation grade of the final elite: the best cell's elite is stored as no_improvement: its cell had an incumbent and neither heldout_verified nor search_only applied, and both of those start from a lower search error than the incumbent's.",
   "rc_thermal saturates near 0.156 for every classical method (see rc_thermal_collapse), so classical held-out RMS values are floored near 0.078; discovered winners break that floor."
